Hospital Information

Emergency admission is used when a patient requires immediate medical attention.

Urgent admission is used when medical treatment is needed quickly but is not necessarily life-threatening.

Elective admission is planned in advance.

Cardiology specializes in heart-related diseases and cardiovascular care.

Neurology specializes in disorders of the nervous system.

Length of Stay is the number of days between Date of Admission and Discharge Date.

Billing Amount represents the amount billed for a patient's hospital treatment.